  "script": "Dual white racing stripes contrast dramatically against metallic gray paint, reminding us of the Shelby GT500's iconic legacy. The carbon fiber rear wing boosts downforce, making the GT500's aerodynamic profile even more aggressive. Check out the dual exhaust system with quad tips, a clear indicator of the GT500 Heritage Edition's raw power. With its striking racing stripes, the Shelby GT500 Heritage Edition pays homage to Ford's unbeatable motorsport origins. Nestled under the hood, the supercharger forces out 760 horsepower and 625 lb-ft of torque. That\u2019s extreme muscle car performance! Inside, Recaro racing seats with the Shelby Cobra emblem offer both support and style, perfect for spirited drives. Carbon fiber accents adorn the dashboard and center console, reinforcing the GT500's focus on performance-oriented design. The GT500's 760 hp eclipses the Chevrolet Camaro ZL1's 650 hp. Plus, the GT500 does the quarter-mile in just 11.0 seconds, quicker than the Camaro. Originally priced around $74K, the GT500 still commands nearly the same figure today, showing its strong demand and lasting legacy. So, would you choose the legendary Shelby GT500 Heritage Edition for its blend of power and tradition? Let us know!",
